<section class="detail-page">
  <p class="back-link"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">← Back to index</a></p>
  <header class="detail-header">
    <div class="detail-eyebrow">
      <span>Pacing benchmark · INGO-sponsored fund first-close timelines</span>
    </div>
    <h1>How long does first close take?</h1>
    <p class="detail-sub">Pacing benchmark for INGO funds mid-raise. The chart plots peer funds with a disclosed first close; filter by profile, enter your announce date for a "you are here" overlay against the median.</p>
    <p class="detail-sub">Two metrics: <em>announce → first close</em> (time on market before LPs locked in; same-day events excluded as pre-arranged) and <em>first close → final close</em> (raising activity past first close). Announce dates are sparser than close dates in the public record, so the first metric's sample is smaller and its median is directional.</p>
  </header>

  <form id="tl-picker" class="picker">
    <fieldset class="picker-group">
      <legend class="picker-legend">Sector tags <span class="picker-hint">— pick the themes your fund will pursue (none = all)</span></legend>
      <div class="picker-chips" data-dim="sectors"></div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="picker-group">
      <legend class="picker-legend">Geography <span class="picker-hint">— pick where your fund will deploy (none = all)</span></legend>
      <div class="picker-chips" data-dim="geos"></div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="picker-group">
      <legend class="picker-legend">Comparables <span class="picker-hint">— include non-INGO funds for sample-size depth</span></legend>
      <div class="picker-chips" data-dim="cohort"></div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="picker-group tl-you-are-here">
      <legend class="picker-legend">You are here <span class="picker-hint">— optional: your own fund's announce date</span></legend>
      <input type="date" id="tl-announce" class="tl-date-input" aria-label="Your fund's announce date" />
      <span id="tl-you-status" class="muted"></span>
      <button type="button" id="tl-clear-you" class="picker-reset">Clear</button>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="picker-actions">
      <button type="button" id="tl-reset" class="picker-reset">Reset filters</button>
      <span id="tl-summary" class="picker-summary"></span>
    </div>
  </form>

  <div class="tl-headlines" id="tl-headlines"></div>

  <ul class="tl-legend" aria-label="Chart legend">
    <li><span class="tl-legend-swatch tl-legend-pre"></span>announce → first close</li>
    <li><span class="tl-legend-swatch tl-legend-post"></span>first close → final close</li>
    <li>
      <svg class="tl-legend-icon" viewBox="-7 -7 14 14" aria-hidden="true">
        <polygon class="tl-bar-sameday" points="-6,0 0,-6 6,0 0,6" />
      </svg>
      same-day announce/close
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg class="tl-legend-icon" viewBox="-6 -6 12 12" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle class="tl-bar-point" r="4.5" />
      </svg>
      first close only — no announce date on file
    </li>
    <li><span class="tl-legend-anchor" aria-hidden="true">⚓</span> anchor LP</li>
    <li><span class="tl-legend-rule tl-legend-rule-median"></span> median (raising-window funds)</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="tl-chart-wrap">
    <div id="tl-chart"></div>
  </div>

  <aside class="tl-method">
    <h3>Method &amp; caveats</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Announce date</strong> means the date the fundraise was first publicly announced (press release, INGO board statement, or partner co-announcement). Where the public record only names the close, announce_date is null.</li>
      <li><strong>First close</strong> is the GP's own reported first close — definitions vary across funds (some report a $5m anchor as "first close," others wait for $50m). The benchmark blurs these. Where size is disclosed it's labeled.</li>
      <li><strong>Survivor bias.</strong> The peer-fund registry only contains funds that announced publicly, and skews toward those that actually reached a close. Funds that quietly died never made the registry. Treat the distribution as an optimistic floor.</li>
      <li><strong>Sample size.</strong> Surfaced loudly per metric. Under sector + geo filter, the working sample often drops below 5 — that's directional only, not a distribution.</li>
    </ul>
  </aside>
</section>

